        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4881226a-c933-5095-b701-cf722f4bc1c3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Margarita Lozano, Luis Buñuel, Sergio Leone, Pier Paolo Pasolini, Taviani brothers, Nanni Moretti, Claude Berri, Marcel Pagnol, Carmelo Gómez, Iciar Bollain, Francisco Algora\n- Films: Viridiana, A Fistful of Dollars, Pigsty, The Night of the Shooting Stars, Kaos, Good Morning Babylon, La messa è finita, Jean de Florette, Manon of the Spring, Manon des Sources, Nos miran, The Chicken\n\nFacts:\n- In 1961, Margarita Lozano worked with Luis Buñuel in the film \"Viridiana.\"\n- In 1964, Margarita Lozano worked with Sergio Leone in the film \"A Fistful of Dollars.\"\n- In 1965, \"The Chicken\" is a French short comedy film directed by Claude Berri.\n- In 1969, Margarita Lozano worked with Pier Paolo Pasolini in the film \"Pigsty.\"\n- Margarita Lozano worked with the Taviani brothers in \"The Night of the Shooting Stars,\" \"Kaos,\" and \"Good Morning Babylon.\"\n- Margarita Lozano worked with Nanni Moretti in \"La messa è finita.\"\n- Margarita Lozano appeared in Claude Berri's two-film adaptation consisting of \"Jean de Florette\" and \"Manon of the Spring.\"\n- \"Manon des Sources\" means \"Manon of the Spring\" and is a 1986 French-language film.\n- \"Manon des Sources\" was directed by Claude Berri and is the second of two films adapted from Marcel Pagnol's 1966 two-volume novel, which Pagnol based on his own earlier film of the same title.\n- \"Nos miran\" is a thriller starring Carmelo Gómez with Iciar Bollain, Margarita Lozano, and Francisco Algora.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
